at the beginning when Chadwick died I  just was completely deflated and I had  no idea how we got back to wakanda  but Ryan is  such an incredibly honest and loving  human being that he pivoted the story to  embrace that loss and he's made it about  exploring grief and how we move on from  great tragedy and in so doing he gave us  as a cast a chance to grieve our brother  and to pay tribute to him in a really  pivotal way and hopefully he's given  permissions for many others to just  handle and and and embrace that grief  process in a more communal way as well
 

